WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.760
Every time I conduct an interview, there’s
always this one test I take for fun!

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.670
I ask the interviewee if they are good at math?

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.230
Some say yes, and some say no!

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.409
And then I break it down a bit.

00:00:14.409 --> 00:00:18.910
Are you comfortable multiplying 2 numbers
and telling me the correct answer?

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.250
Most people say “Oh yes that I definitely
can”

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.980
And then I ask them a super simple multiplication
question like “What’s 4 times 5?”.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.150
Almost everyone answers this correctly.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.111
And then I ask them if they can give me the
answer in 15 seconds.

00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:36.670
They start thinking.

00:00:40.751 --> 00:00:45.140
And just when they’re thinking, I keep a
book and a pen in front of them and tell them

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.060
“Do whatever you want, but get me
the answer in 15 seconds”.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.700
Are you up for the challenge?

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.650
Most people say “Yes let’s do this”.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.300
What’s “7 times 8”?

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.300
Easy!

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.660
What’s “11 times 14”?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.720
Some tell me verbally, some solve it in the
book.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.540
But most people answer in less than 5 seconds!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.700
And now the problems get a little more difficult.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:14.630
A 3 digit number multiplied by a 2 digit number…
or a 3 digit number times a 3 digit number.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.970
Remember, they can do whatever they want,
but the only condition is that they should

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.690
give me the answer in 15 seconds or less!

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.200
Now most people are solving the problems using
a pen and a book but none of them are able

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.420
to give me the answer in less than 15 seconds.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.750
But they don’t give up.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.460
They ask for more problems, and tell me that
they will definitely solve them in less than

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.560
15 seconds.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.560
They fail every time, but they keep trying.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:48.140
I tried this test out with 25 people and 23
of them used the pen and the notebook, and

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.140
failed.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:56.673
But 2 people just took their cellphones out, used a calculator
and gave me the answers in &lt;15s!

00:01:56.673 --> 00:01:59.680
And these 2 were not engineers.

00:01:59.726 --> 00:02:01.630
What did I learn from this?

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.032
Three main things:

00:02:04.032 --> 00:02:07.200
Most people are tense during an interview.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.759
The environment is very controlled.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:12.459
which is why most people are not able to
think rationally.

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:14.659
And the creativity levels drop!

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:20.019
If you’re given things or situations to
solve problems in life, your brain doesn’t

00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:21.660
think beyond them.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.489
Your brain forces you to use them.

00:02:24.578 --> 00:02:30.915
If you’ve been trained to do things in certain
ways, it’s very difficult to think different

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:37.554
If the first 16 years of your life you've been asked to use a pen and a notebook to solve problems,

00:02:37.554 --> 00:02:39.617
then that is what you will do!

00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:42.780
It will be very difficult for you to think out 
of the box.

